  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1209 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nThe mid-week pattern upper ridging over the Rockies and closed \nupper lows on either side of this ridge. Following a secondary \ncold frontal passage Mon night, winds on Tues will shift to \nnortherly, still breezy but not as strong as Monday. A drier \nairmass will be present behind these fronts, with PWATs around \n0.50\" and sfc dewpoints in the 40s, which in conjunction with \nsubtle height rises aloft should keep the FA dry Tues-Wed. The \nwestern-most of these upper lows will swing towards OK on Wed \nnight, but limited moisture return keeps the precip potential low \n(less than 10% in our FA). Another weak cold front associated with\nthis system should provide a renewed push of drier air from the \nnorth, and guidance generally favors upper ridging in the latter \nportions of the forecast period. Thus, mostly dry conditions are \nexpected to continue late week into the weekend. Temps should be \npleasant through the long term forecast period, if not a tad \nchilly, with highs generally in the 60s and lows in the upper 30s \nto upper 40s.",
